# Runtime dependencies for a REMOTE deployment — intent, not the lock.
#
# In remote mode (engine.remote / RELAYTTS_REMOTE_URL) the daemon never loads a
# model: synthesis is an HTTP call to a server that holds the weights. So MLX
# and mlx-audio are deliberately absent — installing them on a remote box costs
# ~2 GB, and leaves a machine able to silently fall back to loading models
# locally, which is the exact memory pressure remote mode exists to avoid.
#
# HTTP goes through urllib from the standard library, so there is no client
# dependency here either.
#
# Regenerate the hash-pinned lockfile after editing:
#
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe --output-file requirements-remote.txt requirements-remote.in
#
# COMPILE THIS WITH PYTHON 3.11 — the version setup_env.sh builds the env with.
# pip-compile resolves against the interpreter running it, so compiling on a
# newer Python silently pins wheels that 3.11 cannot install, and the failure
# only shows up on a fresh deployment:
#
#   ERROR: Could not find a version that satisfies the requirement numpy==2.5.2
#
# ffmpeg (brew install ffmpeg) is still required at runtime: `speed` is honored
# with a pitch-preserving time-stretch locally, on both engines.

soundfile            # decode the WAV the remote server returns; encode the reply
numpy
pyyaml               # the daemon reads config.yaml for voice definitions at startup
